    {# This master switch is deliberately INVISIBLE in the dashboard: its only
       condition in twilight.json compares veloura_product_card_panel_open_2026
       against the sentinel "__veloura_internal_never__", which nothing can ever
       equal, and the field itself declares value/selected = true. In other
       words it is meant to be permanently ON and never shown.

       The fallback here was `false`, which turned that intent upside down:
       a merchant can never switch a hidden field on, so the moment
       theme.settings.get() came back with nothing for it, vpc_enabled went
       false — and vpc_enabled gates EVERYTHING below (the CSS custom
       properties, ~190 rules, and every veloura-product-card-* class on
       <body>). Changing any product-card setting in the dashboard then did
       precisely nothing, because the block that consumes those settings was
       never emitted.

       The fallback now matches the declared value, and matches how the
       identically-hidden veloura_product_page_enabled_2026 is already read in
       pages/product/single.twig. A stored true still reads as true; a missing
       value now also reads as true, which is the documented intent. #}
    {% set vpc_enabled_raw = theme.settings.get('veloura_product_card_enabled_2026', true) %}
    {% if vpc_enabled_raw.value is defined %}
      {% set vpc_enabled_raw = vpc_enabled_raw.value %}
    {% elseif vpc_enabled_raw.selected is defined %}
      {% set vpc_enabled_raw = vpc_enabled_raw.selected %}
    {% endif %}

    {% set vpc_enabled =
      vpc_enabled_raw == true
      or vpc_enabled_raw == 'true'
